WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.397
"The Highest Antioxidant:
Apple, Bean, Berry, Lentil, or Nut?"

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.480
An apple a day has been
associated with as much as

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.760
a 35 percent lower risk
of premature death,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.200
but which apple is best?

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.720
Whichever apple
you'll eat the most.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.520
So, eat your favorite apple.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.200
But if you don't care
which apple you eat,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.360
or you're just curious,

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.880
which apple has the highest
antioxidant content:

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.120
Fuji, Gala, Golden Delicious,
Granny Smith, Pink Lady,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.880
or Red Delicious?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.880
Anytime you want to check the
antioxidant content of foods,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.080
nothing beats this free database
of more than 3,000 foods.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.480
For apples,
Granny gets the gold,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.560
with more than
twice as many antioxidants

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.280
than Golden Delicious apples.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.320
Interestingly, antioxidant
content roughly corresponds

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.320
with the ability
to lower cholesterol levels

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.200
within one month

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.800
for those randomized to eat
an apple a day.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.480
Annurca apples beat
Granny Smith, but presumably,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.200
it's because study participants
got two Annurcas a day

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.440
versus just one of the others,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.800
because they were
about half the size.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.480
But two apples
even when they're half the size,

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.360
have more overall surface area,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.880
and the magic
may be in the peel.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.400
If you randomize people to eat
apples with or without the peel,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.600
you see a significant boost
in artery function

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.040
within an hour
of peel consumption.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.640
So, don't peel your apples.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.840
For other foods, the antioxidant
spread can be even greater.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.200
Check out nuts.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.240
Two nuts pull way ahead,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.200
with the top nut having nearly
75 times the antioxidants

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.160
than the bottom nut.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.920
Which do you think is which?

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.600
Want to pause and guess?

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.360
Walnuts for the win!

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.880
Followed by pecans,
then pistachios,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.720
and who would have guessed
almonds would be

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.040
way down here at the bottom?

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.640
Walnuts also have
the highest omega-3 content,

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.960
by a large margin,
beat out other nuts

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.740
in suppressing the growth
of cancer cells

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.120
in a Petri dish.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.120
And walnuts are
the only nuts shown

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.960
to markedly improve
human artery function.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.240
Blackberries
beat out blueberries

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.320
for antioxidant capacity.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.040
The beans surprised me.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.200
What do you think fits the bill
for best bean,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.120
at least
from an antioxidant perspective?

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.880
Want to pause and take bets?

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.040
The lowest on the leaderboard:

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.280
chickpeas.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.640
Holy hummus!

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.440
The mightiest free radical
fighter is the fava bean,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.240
with kidneys and pintos
neck and neck for number two.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.880
Lentils were
another big surprise.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.960
I would have guessed
black or red lentils

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.760
to be up there with brown
or green at the bottom.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.640
But check this out.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.720
Green lentils have
about four times

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.498
the antioxidant power
of red ones!

